[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_pretense.py: Implement SemVer solver interface pretense state machine: concrete domains for all 9 VersionEngine/PackageRepository/DependencySolver transitions, model state for parsed versions/ranges, registered releases and resolutions, error-free precondition gating, synthesized fake factory, full fixed fake transition coverage tests, and fake Hypothesis stateful fuzzing.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: Implement SemVer solver implementation pretense pseudo-state machine: call_target pivots and postcondition asserts for all 9 interface transitions without new state classes, require guards, or state mutation; real implementation tests driving as_checked proxies across parsing, precedence, ranges, satisfaction, repository registration/query ordering, and dependency resolution; real SUT Hypothesis stateful fuzzing.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver.py: Implement SemVer 2.0 interface: dataclass exceptions with message/raw attributes and __str__, frozen data types (Version with is_prerelease/format/__str__, VersionRange, PackageDependency, PackageRelease, ResolutionOutcome), comparator enum, and flat Protocol stubs for VersionEngine, PackageRepository, and DependencySolver matching low/semver_solver.pyi.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: Implement SemVer 2.0 services: regex-validated parse_version with leading-zero rejection, precedence comparison (numeric/prerelease, build ignored), range parsing into DNF with basic comparators, caret/tilde prefixes, wildcards, hyphen ranges, unions, operator whitespace and validation errors; PackageRepository with descending release indexing and PackageNotFoundError; DependencySolver with MRV depth-first backtracking, forward checking, conflict trail, prerelease-aware matching, and ResolutionConflictError for unregistered or unsatisfiable packages.
[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_pretense.py: [slug:semver.solver.compatible_assignment] [viol:pret_qa.uncontracted_state_rule] Facet: resolve root-dependency argument domain Witness: transition='DependencySolver.resolve', domain='Domain.sampled_from(candidates)' The DependencySolver.resolve transition builds the root_dependencies argument domain from a candidates list assembled as a method-local variable inside the transition body, so Pretense domain evaluation cannot resolve that name and raises NameError: name 'candidates' is not defined before the transition executes. Every fuzzing sequence reaching resolve therefore crashes during argument generation instead of exercising the contracted compatible-assignment behavior, and the claimed concrete domains for all nine transitions leave resolve without a resolvable state-derived argument domain.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_pretense.py: Resolve feedback: replace the transition-local candidates list (unresolvable by Pretense domain evaluation) with a state-derived argument domain. Model state now tracks dependency_options as a list of resolvable root-dependency sets; register_package appends the empty set and a satisfiable single-package constraint for each registered release, and resolve gates root_dependencies via Domain.in_set(self.state.dependency_options), so fuzz generation resolves the domain at generation time, never raises NameError, and only offers dependency sets whose packages exist in the repository mirror.
