[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: [slug:semver.parse_range.bare_partials_prohibited] [viol:pret_cov.transition_frequency_starvation] Facet: unreached contract violations and range algebra scenarios Witness: errors='InvalidVersionError,InvalidRangeError,PackageNotFoundError,ResolutionConflictError'. The deterministic scenario suite only drives happy-path parses and two trivial resolutions, so contracted precondition-violation transitions are never reached: no scenario drives a leading-zero or grammar-violating version string into InvalidVersionError; no scenario drives an empty or whitespace-only range, a bare partial version, a comma-delimited comparator list, an empty union clause, or a spaced relational operator into InvalidRangeError; no scenario queries an unregistered package name to provoke PackageNotFoundError; and no scenario resolves an unregistered or unsatisfiable dependency graph to provoke ResolutionConflictError. The positive-path contract is also starved: numeric patch-number ordering and prerelease identifier ordering (numeric vs numeric, numeric vs string, string vs string, and longer shared-prefix sequences) are unexercised, as are the contracted range algebra cases for wildcard comparator expansions, caret and tilde prefix boundaries over both full and wildcard versions, both bounds of hyphen ranges, and transitive dependency resolution where forward checking rejects an already assigned package and the search must backtrack to a lower-precedence release. Every one of these is an explicit postcondition or error-bearing precondition of the low-level specification and must be reached by deterministic scenario transitions.
[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: [slug:semver.parse_range.malformed_syntax] [viol:cov.unreachable_under_spec] Facet: dead malformed comparator error guard Witness: lines='289-294', condition='prefix_match is None never holds'. The guard at lines 289-294 in this file is structurally unreachable under the contracted range grammar: tokens are produced by whitespace splitting so each token is non-empty, and the comparator-prefix pattern accepts every non-empty token (the operator group is optional and the remaining group matches any non-empty text), so the None branch can never be taken and the InvalidRangeError raise at line 291 never executes for any input that reaches it. No conforming call sequence into range parsing can enter this branch; malformed comparator text is already rejected downstream by the version and wildcard validation paths in this same file. Because this branch is no-op dead code under the specification closure, either prune the raise and the redundant None check, replace it with an unreachable() marker from pretense, or annotate the guard with a '# pragma: no cover (assumption: ...)' comment stating why the token scan cannot produce an unparsable token.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: Address unreachable-guard feedback: prune the dead malformed-comparator InvalidRangeError branch in _compile_clause. The optional-group prefix regex is replaced by an explicit longest-first operator-prefix scan (_COMPARATOR_PREFIXES), so every non-empty whitespace-delimited token is partitioned into an operator plus target with no structurally unreachable None branch; malformed targets are still rejected downstream by the version and wildcard validation paths. Comparator parsing behavior is preserved (>, >=, <, <=, =, ==, !=, ^, ~ prefixes unchanged), and the now-unused _COMPARATOR_PREFIX_RE is removed.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: Resolve coverage-starvation feedback by expanding the deterministic real scenario suite: assert InvalidVersionError for leading-zero and grammar-violating version strings, InvalidRangeError for empty/whitespace ranges, bare partials across comparators and hyphens, comma-delimited comparators, and empty union clauses, PackageNotFoundError for unregistered names, and ResolutionConflictError for unregistered and unsatisfiable dependency graphs; plus positive-path coverage for numeric patch ordering, prerelease identifier ordering (numeric/numeric, numeric/string, string/string, shared-prefix length), build metadata exclusion, wildcard comparator expansions (>=1.x, !=1.x, >=*), caret and tilde boundaries over full and wildcard versions, both bounds of hyphen ranges (full, wildcard upper, both wildcard), spaced-operator equivalence, prerelease range filtering, plain transitive resolution, and transitive backtracking to a lower-precedence release when forward checking rejects the highest lib release.
