[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: [slug:semver.parse_range.malformed_syntax] [viol:pret_cov.transition_frequency_starvation] Facet: malformed wildcard and dangling operator rejections Witness: tokens='1.2.3.4, 1.x.2, 1.zz, 1.02.x, >='. The contracted malformed-syntax rejections for wildcard expressions remain unexercised: no scenario supplies a token with more than three dot-separated components, a numeric component that follows a wildcard component, a component that is neither numeric nor a wildcard, a numeric component carrying a leading zero, or a trailing operator left without a following target. Each of these is malformed range text for which the specification requires InvalidRangeError, so the corresponding terminal violation transitions are still missing from the deterministic scenario suite.
[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: [slug:semver.parse_range.comparators_and_prefixes] [viol:pret_cov.transition_frequency_starvation] Facet: comparator and wildcard boundary expansions Witness: ranges='!=1.0.0, <=1.0.0, >1.0.0, 1.x, >1.x, <1.x, <=1.x, >*, ^0.1.2, ^0.0.3, x - 2.x'. The range algebra postconditions remain partially unexercised: the !=, <=, and > forms applied to a full version; the bare, exclusive-upper, exclusive-lower, and inclusive-upper forms applied to a two-component wildcard; an impossible relational or negated form applied to a fully wildcard expression; caret boundaries where the major component is zero and the first non-zero component must determine the upper bound; the upper boundary of a two-component wildcard; and a hyphen range whose bound is fully wildcard. These are contracted comparator, prefix, wildcard, and hyphen expansions, and every one is reachable from a fixed range expression that the specification declares valid.
[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: [slug:semver.compare_precedence.prerelease_ordering] [viol:pret_cov.transition_frequency_starvation] Facet: reverse numeric versus alphanumeric identifier rank Witness: pair='1.0.0-alpha vs 1.0.0-1'. The contracted prerelease ordering holds that numeric identifiers rank below alphanumeric identifiers, but the scenario suite only exercises the direction in which the left-hand identifier is numeric and the right-hand identifier is alphanumeric. The reverse orientation, with the numerically-typed identifier in the right-hand position, is unexercised, so the contracted asymmetric ranking between numeric and alphanumeric prerelease segments is only half reached.
[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: [slug:semver.solver.unsatisfiable_conflict] [viol:pret_cov.transition_frequency_starvation] Facet: forward checking conflict and nested search exhaustion Witness: graph='root: B==1.0.0 and A==1.0.0; A 1.0.0 depends on B>=2.0.0'. The contracted unsatisfiable-conflict behavior is currently only reached for a single root package with no viable release; no scenario drives forward checking to reject an already assigned package when a later-selected release declares a dependency range that the existing assignment violates, and no scenario exhausts every candidate of an outer package after a nested branch fails and unwinds. Those two transitions are the ones that must raise ResolutionConflictError populated with the conflicting package names and a derivation explanation, and both are reachable with a fixed dependency graph that the specification allows.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: Address third coverage round: add malformed wildcard/operator rejections (1.2.3.4, 1.x.2, 1.zz, 1.02.x, trailing >=) to InvalidRangeError scenarios; add a comparator/wildcard boundary scenario covering !=/<=/> full-version comparators, bare and >1.x/<1.x/<=1.x two-component wildcard forms, impossible >* and !=* fully-wildcard forms, zero-major caret boundaries (^0.1.2, ^0.0.3), the two-component wildcard upper boundary, and the fully-wildcard hyphen bound (x - 2.x); add the reverse numeric-versus-alphanumeric prerelease comparison (1.0.0-1 below 1.0.0-alpha); and add forward-checking conflict and nested-search-exhaustion conflict scenarios that assert ResolutionConflictError carries non-empty conflicting_packages and explanation.
